### Page 4 of 6

```text
TO: Lt. Rob Dafoe
Cheyenne Police Department Memorandum
Protecting the Legend
FROM: Lewis Simpson, Equipment Quartermaster
SUBJECT: Sole Source ~~irement for Motorola Radios
DATE: April 13, 2018 ~
••••••••••••••••• ••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••• •
The Cheyenne Police Department radio inventory of over 375 units is currently 100%
Motorola and therefore to maintain continuity and officer safety, Motorola must continue
to be the sole source for all radios.
The Cheyenne Police Department currently uses as its primary radio communication
system, the WyoLink Trunked Radio System (WyoLink) as maintained by the State of
Wyoming. While other manufacturer radios have been tested, and certified for use on the
WyoLink system, the Cheyenne Police Department has determined that the Motorola
radio equipment certified for use on the WyoLink system provides the best operational
reliability to meet the departments mission to provide the best public safety to the
community and has relied on that dependability for many years.
Departmental Memorandum
- 1 -
```

### Page 5 of 6

```text
Monday, April 16, 2018
Lew Simpson
City of Cheyenne Police Department
415 W. 18Th Street
Cheyenne, WY 82001
RE: WAC/Motorola Sole Source
Lew,
This letter is to confirm that WAC/Motorola is the certified communications vendor for the City of
Cheyenne Police Department and the other municipalities in the State of Wyoming. WAC is authorized by
Motorola to offer pricing on communications equipment using the pre-negotiated Wyolink Contract price.
I would be pleased to address any concerns the City of Cheyenne Police Department may have regarding
this letter. Any questions can be directed to me at 970-590-3461 or weschisnall@wiradcom.com.
Sincerely,
Wes Chisnall
Government Market Account Manager
```

### Page 6 of 6

```text
REQUEST TO PURCHASE OVER $35,000.00
The City of Cheyenne requests to purchase Motorola Dual-Band APX7500 Complete Vehicle 2-
way Radio Systems and chargers, for the Cheyenne Police Department from Wireless Advanced
Communications, Evans, CO in the amount of $87,714.60. This is a single source purchase,
therefore no bids were requested.
This will be reviewed by City Council at Finance on May 7, 2018 and voted on
at the May 14, 2018 City Council meeting.
If you have any questions, please call Sara Vasquez at 307/637-6345.
Sara Vasquez
Purchasing Manager
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WY
Published in: Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
Dates:
April 19 and 26, 2018
```
